# A headless display for the in-guest `screenshot` tool (DESIGN-BOXES 2(g)):
# chromium for url mode, Xvfb + scrot (and Pillow for the downscale) for app
# mode. About +450 MB. chromium peaks at 300-500 MB, hence the memory floor:
# on a 4 GB host the RAM budget then keeps it from running beside another
# large box.
#
# The live desktop (guest/backend/display.py, docs/desktop.md) adds a VNC X
# server (tigervnc), a window manager (openbox), a terminal on a tmux session
# (xterm, tmux) and the input/capture tools the agent drives it with (xdotool,
# maim): about +60 MB. httpx and textual are the jav3 terminal client's own
# libraries, baked in so it can be tried in the box without PyPI egress (pip
# lines land in the /opt/jav3/py venv, which run_code and the desktop terminal
# put first on PATH). The recipe takes exact pins only; both sit inside
# clients/jav3cli/install.sh's ranges (httpx>=0.27,<1; textual>=8,<9), which
# tests/test_desktop_display.py checks.
name desktop
from main
min_mem_mb 1280

apt xvfb chromium fonts-dejavu-core scrot matchbox-window-manager
apt python3-pil
apt tigervnc-standalone-server xterm openbox xdotool maim tmux
pip httpx==0.28.1 textual==8.2.8
